@page "/legal/privacy"
@attribute [ExcludeFromInteractiveRouting]
@layout MarketingLayout
@using Microsoft.Extensions.Options
@inject IOptions<CompanyOptions> CompanyOptions

<PageTitle>Privacy Policy · Drive-In Online</PageTitle>

<MarketingNav />
<PageHero Eyebrow="Legal" Title="Privacy Policy" Lede="@($"Effective {C.EffectiveDate}")" />

<main class="wrap page">
    <div class="prose">
        <LegalDraftBanner />

        <p>
            This policy explains what personal information Drive-In Online (provided by @C.Name, "we") collects, how we use it, and your choices.
            For tickets, the theater you buy from also receives your information and handles it under its own policies.
        </p>

        <h2>What we collect</h2>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>Account information:</strong> your email address, display name, and a salted hash of your password (never the password itself).
                If you sign in with Google, we receive your email address and whether Google has verified it.</li>
            <li><strong>Theater information:</strong> what owners and staff enter: the theater's profile, screens, schedule, prices, and staff
                names, email addresses and roles.</li>
            <li><strong>Ticket purchases:</strong> the showing, spot, ticket options and add-ons, amount, time of purchase, the email address the
                receipt goes to, and gate check-in times. For card payments we keep only the card brand and last four digits; the full card
                number goes to the payment processor and isn't stored by us.</li>
            <li><strong>Technical information:</strong> server logs with IP addresses, browser type and the pages requested, kept to operate and
                secure the Service.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Cookies</h2>
        <p>
            We use only cookies needed for the Service to work: to keep you signed in and to protect forms against forgery. We don't use
            advertising or analytics cookies. Our pages load fonts from Google Fonts, which receives your IP address when you visit.
        </p>

        <h2>How we use it</h2>
        <ul>
            <li>to provide the Service: sign-in, running theaters, selling and checking tickets, and sending receipts, invitations and account emails;</li>
            <li>to bill theaters for their subscriptions;</li>
            <li>to keep the Service secure, prevent fraud and abuse, and fix problems;</li>
            <li>to meet legal obligations.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>We don't sell personal information, and we don't use it for advertising.</p>

        <h2>Who we share it with</h2>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>Theaters:</strong> when you buy a ticket, the theater sees your purchase and receipt email. Staff see what their roles allow.</li>
            <li><strong>Service providers</strong> who process data for us: Amazon Web Services (hosting, database, backups and email delivery),
                Google (if you choose Google sign-in), and our payment processor (card payments).</li>
            <li><strong>When the law requires it,</strong> or to protect the rights and safety of users, theaters or the public.</li>
            <li><strong>In a business transfer,</strong> such as a merger or sale, subject to this policy.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
        <p>
            Account information is kept while your account exists. Ticket sales are kept as the theater's business records. Database backups are
            kept for 30 days. Server logs are kept only as long as needed to operate and secure the Service.
        </p>

        <h2>Your choices</h2>
        <ul>
            <li>Update your email address and password under your account settings.</li>
            <li>Download your personal data, or delete your account, under Account → Personal data. Tickets you bought stay with the theater as
                sales records but are no longer linked to your account.</li>
            <li>Depending on where you live, you may have other rights, such as to access or correct your information; contact us to use them.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Security</h2>
        <p>
            Connections are encrypted, passwords are hashed, and access to data is limited to what's needed to run the Service. No system is
            perfectly secure; if a breach affects your information, we'll notify you as the law requires.
        </p>

        <h2>Children</h2>
        <p>The Service isn't directed to children under 13, and we don't knowingly collect their personal information.</p>

        <h2>Changes</h2>
        <p>We'll post any changes here with a new effective date, and email account holders about material changes.</p>

        <h2>Contact</h2>
        <p>@C.Name · @C.Address · <ContactLink /></p>
    </div>
</main>

<MarketingFooter />

@code {
    private CompanyOptions C => CompanyOptions.Value;
}
